अवकृश् अव-कृश्, Caus. -कर्शयति, -यितुम्,
to emaciate, make lean or meagre or mean-looking;
to deform.

अवकॄ अव-कॄ, cl. 6. P. -किरति, -करितुम्,
[]
-रीतुम्, to pour out or down, to spread, to scatter;
to shake off, throw off, leave; to bestrew, pour upon,
cover with, fill: A. -किरते, to extend; to fall asunder;
to pass away, fall off, become faithless.

अव-ग्राह, अस्, m. breaking off, discontinuing;
obstacle, impediment, imprecation; drought; the
forehead of an elephant.

अवतन् अव-तन्, cl. 8. P. -तनोति, -नितुम्,
to stretch or extend downwards; to overspread, cover;
to loosen, undo, especially a bowstring.

अवदात अव-दात, अस्, आ, अम्, or अव-दातक,
अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. दै with अव), clean, clear;
white; yellow; beautiful; (अस्), m. white colour.

अव-धूनन, अम्, n. shaking, causing to shake;
expelling; agitation, trembling; trampling on, tread-
ing on.

अव-मर्दन, अस्, आ, अम्, treading down, grind-
ing, crushing, oppressing; (अम्), n. rubbing, washing;
oppression.

अवस, अम्, n., Ved. refreshment, food, provisions,
viaticum; preserving, protecting; (अस्), m. a king;
the sun.

अव-सन्न, अस्, आ, अम्, sunk down, bowed, bent;
languid, enervated; melancholy, dispirited, unhappy;
ended, terminated, separated; non-suited.
—अव-
सन्न-ता, f. or अवसन्न-त्व, अम्, n. affliction,
low spirits; dejection; termination, completion.

अव-सादन, अम्, n. oppressing, disheartening;
finishing; an escharotic; removing proud flesh by
escharotic applications.

अव-हरण, अम्, n. throwing away; taking away;
stealing, plundering; taking back, redeeming; fining,
mulcting.

अवाचीन, अस्, आ, अम्, down-looked, headlong;
south, southern; descended, gone down; (अस्), m.,
N. of a king.
